# Per-machine configuration for the "lucap workstation" (ZWorkstation, Ubuntu).
# ONE file for all three runtimes: iomp and libgomp compile and run on the
# host; pmsis cross-compiles riscv32 and builds+runs through the PULP-SDK
# harness Makefile on gvsoc. The PULP_* variables at the bottom are only used
# when RUNTIME=pmsis and are ignored by the native runtimes.
#
# To use it, copy it to `config.env` (same directory):
#   cp config.env.lucap-workstation.example config.env
#
# `config.env` is git-ignored, so your local paths never get committed.
# Anything you export in your shell before running the script overrides these:
#   RUNTIME=pmsis DATASET=MINI_DATASET ./run_performance.sh

# --- Tool directories (prepended to PATH if set) ---------------------------
# LLVM/CIR tools (clang-cir, cir-opt, mlir-opt, mlir-translate) come from the
# shared read-only install; mlir-opt-omp from this user's own checkout build
# (OMP_TOOL_BIN is prepended after LLVM_BIN, so it wins over any mlir-opt-omp
# living in the shared install).
LLVM_BIN="/home/tagliavini/MLIR/INSTALL-LLVM/bin"
OMP_TOOL_BIN="$HOME/mlir-opt-omp/build"

# --- Individual tool overrides (optional) ----------------------------------
# Only needed if a tool is not reachable via the dirs above / your PATH,
# or to pin a specific version (e.g. the libgomp reference compiler).
# CLANG=clang
# GCC=gcc-12
# OPT=opt
# LLC=llc
# CIR_OPT=cir-opt
# MLIR_OPT=mlir-opt
# MLIR_TRANSLATE=mlir-translate
# MLIR_OPT_OMP=mlir-opt-omp

# --- Paths -----------------------------------------------------------------
POLYBENCH="$HOME/PolyBenchC-4.2.1-OpenMP"
# POLYBENCH_UTIL="$POLYBENCH/utilities"     # defaults to $POLYBENCH/utilities
RULES="$HOME/mlir-opt-omp/rules.dsl"        # same checkout as the tool build
# OpenMP headers used by the clang->CIR front-end (workstation ships gcc-12):
INC_OMP="/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/12/include"
# OUTDIR="$PWD/results"                      # where binaries/dumps/CSV land
#                                            # (a <runtime>/ subdir is appended)

# --- Run parameters --------------------------------------------------------
RUNTIME="iomp"            # iomp | libgomp | pmsis (pulp/gvsoc)
DATASET="LARGE_DATASET"   # MINI_/SMALL_/STANDARD_/LARGE_/EXTRALARGE_DATASET
                          # (pmsis: use MINI_DATASET — GAP8 memory is tiny and
                          #  it must match the harness Makefile's native builds)
THREADS="16"              # threads for parallel runs (ignored on pmsis: the
                          # core count is fixed by the harness NUM_CORES)
SUITE="full"              # full: run the whole external PolyBench suite (29 kernels)
# KERNELS="linear-algebra/blas/gemm/gemm-omp.c ..."  # explicit list overrides SUITE

# --- Performance-only parameters (run_performance.sh) -----------------------
# REPS="5"                  # timed runs per cell (pmsis: always 1, gvsoc is deterministic)
# VARIANCE_ACCEPTED="5"     # warn if a cell's relative std-dev exceeds this %
PLOT="true"               # render results/<runtime>/results_performance_<sel>.png at
                          # the end (per-kernel speedup bars for the SUITE that
                          # ran; needs python3 + matplotlib — see plot_speedup.py)
# The plot uses the local venv ./.venv automatically if present; create it once:
#   python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install matplotlib numpy
# PLOT_PYTHON=""            # or point at any python with matplotlib

# =============================================================================
# PULP / gvsoc — everything below is only used when RUNTIME=pmsis
# =============================================================================
# The PolyBench checkout doubles as the PULP-SDK harness: its Makefile supports
#   make clean all run platform=gvsoc KERNEL_SRC=... [OMP_NATIVE=1|OMP_OPT=1]
# and prints 'Cycles = N' after the run.
PULP_APP_DIR="$POLYBENCH"
# GAP RISC-V GCC toolchain used by the PULP-SDK make (prepended to PATH):
PULP_TOOLCHAIN_BIN="/home/tagliavini/toolchains/gap_riscv_toolchain_ubuntu/INSTALL/bin"
# GAP SDK environment, sourced automatically by common.sh. Alternatively
# comment this out and source it yourself before running:
PULP_SDK_ENV="/home/tagliavini/gap8/gap_sdk/configs/gap8_v3.sh"
# riscv32-capable LLVM opt/llc (xpulpv backend) that produce kernel.o — a
# different LLVM install than the host tools above:
PULP_OPT="/home/tagliavini/toolchains/llvm-project/builds/INSTALL-REBASE/bin/opt"
PULP_LLC="/home/tagliavini/toolchains/llvm-project/builds/INSTALL-REBASE/bin/llc"
# PULP_OPT_FLAGS=""         # host 'opt' pass on the .ll; none by default
# PULP_LLC_FLAGS="-O3 -mtriple=riscv32-unknown-elf -mattr=+m,+c,+xpulpv -relocation-model=pic"
# PULP_PLATFORM="gvsoc"     # gvsoc | board
# Path (relative to PULP_APP_DIR) of the linked ELF, used for the size columns:
# PULP_BUILD_BIN="BUILD/GAP8_V3/GCC_RISCV_PULPOS/test"
# PolyBench defines baked into the opt kernel.o — MUST match what the harness
# Makefile defines for the native builds:
# PULP_POLYBENCH_DEFS="-DPOLYBENCH_DUMP_ARRAYS -DPOLYBENCH_TIME"
# PULP_VERBOSE=1            # stream the make/gvsoc output instead of logging only
